# prose-audit: Grade C — Desk framing is fine, but both conflicts beneath it are skeletal: the congress and the EU-primacy ruling each get a one-sentence premise with no named actors (no Przyłębska, no Ziobro, no Commission), and all seven outcomes close on an abstract one-paragraph verdict ("the constitutional fight gains a front") instead of naming who won, lost or now owns it.
