@oct21_pawlowska
# prose-audit: Grade A — The event distinguishes Pawłowska's March move into Gowin's party from her October entry into the PiS club, treats the lost mandate as Wiosna's organisational wound and gives every possible leading Left current its own voice.
title: From Wiosna to the PiS club
subtitle: One of Wiosna's 2019 mandates completes its journey across the chamber
face-image: img/poland/events/sejm-new-deputies-2023.webp
new-page: true
view-if: october_2021_pawlowska_done = 0 and party_unity <= 70
on-arrival: {!
const firstVisit = Number(Q.october_2021_pawlowska_done) !== 1;
Q.october_2021_pawlowska_done = 1;
if (firstVisit) {
    Q.left_seats = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.left_seats) || 0) - 1);
    Q.left_spring_seats = Math.max(
        0, (Number(Q.left_spring_seats) || 0) - 1
    );
    Q.nowa_lewica_seats = Math.max(
        0, (Number(Q.nowa_lewica_seats) || 0) - 1
    );
    Q.pis_seats = Math.max(0, Number(Q.pis_seats) || 0) + 1;
    Q.spring_estimated_mps = Math.max(
        0, (Number(Q.spring_estimated_mps) || 0) - 1
    );
    Q.spring_individual_defections =
        Math.max(0, Number(Q.spring_individual_defections) || 0) + 1;
    Q.spring_mp_departed =
        Math.max(0, Number(Q.spring_mp_departed) || 0) + 1;
    Q.party_unity = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.party_unity) || 0) - 5);
    Q.spring_dissent =
        Math.max(0, (Number(Q.spring_dissent) || 0) + 6);
}
Q.pawlowska_response_actor =
    Q.left_dominant_current == "spring" ? "Wiosna's leadership" :
    (Q.left_dominant_current == "razem" ? "Razem's leadership" :
        (Q.left_dominant_current == "barons" ? "The SLD executive" :
            (Q.left_dominant_current == "members"
                ? "The member executive"
                : "The federal council")));
Q.pawlowska_response = "Unanswered";
Q.news_headline =
    "Former Wiosna MP Monika Pawłowska joins the PiS parliamentary club";
!}

= October 2021 — One mandate, three affiliations

**Monika Pawłowska** entered the Sejm in 2019 as a Wiosna candidate on the
Lewica list and became a deputy chair of our parliamentary club. On 21 March
she left both Wiosna and the club for **Jarosław Gowin's Porozumienie**, saying
that it offered sincere cooperation across party lines. She joined the party
but initially remained an unaffiliated deputy rather than entering the PiS
club.

Six months later Gowin is outside the United Right and Pawłowska is outside
Porozumienie. On 1 October she announces that, after speaking to **Jarosław
Kaczyński** and **Mateusz Morawiecki**, she is joining the **PiS parliamentary
club**. The Left has lost one seat; PiS has gained one. The journey matters
because it began inside Wiosna, not inside an anonymous common list.

[? if left_dominant_current = "spring": Wiosna leads this project. Calling the
move somebody else's discipline problem is therefore impossible: she was our
regional organiser, our candidate and our deputy before she was Gowin's.?]
[? if left_dominant_current = "razem": Razem leads the common project, but the
candidate came through Wiosna's organisation. Our response can impose a common
standard without rewriting which current recruited her.?]
[? if left_dominant_current = "barons": The SLD executive controls the party,
but Pawłowska was not an SLD-machine deputy. Central discipline can answer the
loss only by taking responsibility for a Wiosna recruitment decision.?]
[? if left_dominant_current = "members": The member executive was created to
stand above inherited components. This is the first case in which that promise
requires it to examine one of them in public.?]
[? if left_dominant_current != "spring" and left_dominant_current != "razem"
and left_dominant_current != "barons" and left_dominant_current != "members":
No current owns the whole alliance. Wiosna supplied the candidate, while the
common list supplied the mandate and neither can answer alone.?]

- @pawlowska_audit
- @pawlowska_pledge
- @pawlowska_pis

@pawlowska_audit
title: [+ pawlowska_response_actor +] opens Wiosna's Lubelskie files
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Treat the defection as an organisational failure before treating it as a television line.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: There is no spare capacity for interviews, membership records and a regional review.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.resources) || 0) - 1);
Q.pawlowska_response = "Wiosna recruitment audit";
Q.spring_dissent = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.spring_dissent) || 0) - 5);
Q.party_unity = Math.min(100, (Number(Q.party_unity) || 0) + 1);
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 3;
Q.media_capacity = (Number(Q.media_capacity) || 0) + 1;
Q.news_headline =
    "Lewica opens Wiosna's candidate files after Pawłowska's defection";
!}

The review starts in Chełm and Lublin, not in a Warsaw studio. The regional
membership roll, the 2019 selection interviews and every warning sent to the
national office are opened to representatives of the current that now leads
the party.

[? if left_dominant_current = "spring": Biedroń signs the report himself.
Wiosna loses the defence that one ambitious deputy deceived everybody, but it
keeps the right to show that it can correct its own recruitment.?]
[? if left_dominant_current = "razem": Razem publishes the selection criteria
it wanted in 2019 beside the ones Wiosna actually used. The lesson is real; so
is the suspicion that a rival current has turned an audit into a verdict.?]
[? if left_dominant_current = "barons": The SLD executive finds failures and
also finds an opportunity to centralise candidate approval. Wiosna accepts the
report and starts guarding what remains of its autonomy.?]
[? if left_dominant_current = "members": The member executive holds an open
hearing rather than a factional trial. It is slower, but no inherited current
gets to mark its own work.?]
[? if left_dominant_current != "spring" and left_dominant_current != "razem"
and left_dominant_current != "barons" and left_dominant_current != "members":
The federal council lets Wiosna supply the record and the other parties supply
the questions. Nobody can call the finding a purge.?]

The event still leaves the party less united than it was before the mandate
crossed the chamber. What the audit restores is the possibility of learning
from the loss.

- @october_2021_hub: File the report

@pawlowska_pledge
title: [+ pawlowska_response_actor +] writes a mandate-and-list pledge
subtitle: Every current must state what an MP owes the voters who supplied the list, without pretending a party can legally own a mandate.
on-arrival: {!
Q.pawlowska_response = "Common mandate-and-list pledge";
Q.party_unity = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.party_unity) || 0) - 2);
// internal_dissent is recomputed from the caucus record every month, so
// the grievance has to land on the caucuses themselves.
Q.spring_dissent = (Number(Q.spring_dissent) || 0) + 2;
Q.progressives_dissent = (Number(Q.progressives_dissent) || 0) + 2;
Q.constitutional_restraint =
    (Number(Q.constitutional_restraint) || 0) + 2;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 1;
Q.news_headline =
    "Every Left current signs a common pledge on mandates and defections";
!}

The document does not claim that the seat belongs to Wiosna; the constitution
does not make deputies delegates of a party. It says something narrower: a
candidate who changes camps must face their voters, disclose every negotiation
and seek a place on the new party's list at the next election without a
protected transfer.

[? if left_dominant_current = "spring": Wiosna accepts the first signature
because the breach was its own. The pledge steadies the organisation and makes
every other deputy wonder which private conversation will next require a
public explanation.?]
[? if left_dominant_current = "razem": Razem gets the common ethical rule it
wanted without acquiring a legal power to recall MPs. Wiosna signs, then asks
why a rival had to draft its answer.?]
[? if left_dominant_current = "barons": The SLD executive turns an ethical
pledge into a whip's instrument within hours. Discipline improves on paper and
every smaller current starts keeping its own copy of the candidate list.?]
[? if left_dominant_current = "members": The member executive makes the
pledge reciprocal: leaders who change the programme must explain themselves as
fully as deputies who change the club.?]
[? if left_dominant_current != "spring" and left_dominant_current != "razem"
and left_dominant_current != "barons" and left_dominant_current != "members":
The federal parties sign the same words under separate logos. The standard is
common even where the organisations are not.?]

The pledge cannot return Pawłowska's vote. It makes the next departure harder
to describe as a private act with no debt to the list that made it possible.

- @october_2021_hub: Publish the pledge

@pawlowska_pis
title: [+ pawlowska_response_actor +] makes this a PiS-majority story
subtitle: Attack Kaczyński's recruitment and refuse an inquiry into how Wiosna chose the deputy he recruited.
on-arrival: {!
Q.pawlowska_response = "Attack on PiS recruitment";
Q.party_unity = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.party_unity) || 0) - 1);
Q.spring_dissent = (Number(Q.spring_dissent) || 0) + 3;
Q.pis_relation = (Number(Q.pis_relation) || 0) - 6;
Q.media_capacity = (Number(Q.media_capacity) || 0) + 2;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) - 1;
Q.news_headline =
    "Lewica asks what PiS promised for one more parliamentary vote";
!}

Our speakers ask what was offered, who made the first call and why a governing
club that claims an ample majority is recruiting one deputy at a time. PiS has
to answer the arithmetic instead of celebrating the transfer.

[? if left_dominant_current = "spring": Because Wiosna leads the response,
every interviewer asks the question we omitted: how did its own regional
coordinator become available for recruitment in the first place??]
[? if left_dominant_current = "razem": Razem's attack is sharp and familiar.
Wiosna hears it as a rival using one of its losses to prove an old argument
about candidate selection.?]
[? if left_dominant_current = "barons": The SLD executive keeps the cameras on
Kaczyński and quietly takes candidate vetting back into headquarters. Wiosna
notices the second move even if the public does not.?]
[? if left_dominant_current = "members": The member executive refuses to
invent evidence of a bargain, so the attack ends as a list of unanswered
questions rather than an accusation it cannot prove.?]
[? if left_dominant_current != "spring" and left_dominant_current != "razem"
and left_dominant_current != "barons" and left_dominant_current != "members":
The federal council agrees on the attack and on nothing about responsibility.
Each component leaves the studio believing another one should conduct the
review.?]

The line lasts a news cycle. The missing mandate and Wiosna's unanswered
recruitment question last longer.

- @october_2021_hub: Return to the October desk

@oct21_eu
# prose-audit: Grade B — Przyłębska, Ziobro, the Commission and the recovery money now stand behind the ruling, each route names who owns the consequence, and the material route is visibly locked to the December 2020 veto position; the judges who dissented are still unnamed.
