    (Number(Q.constitutional_conflict_level) || 0) + 15;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Tribunal rules that parts of the EU treaties are unconstitutional";
!}

= October 2021 — Which legal order?

The Constitutional Tribunal under **Julia Przyłębska** — a court whose own
composition is disputed, ruling on a question referred to it by the government
that appointed most of it — holds that parts of the European treaties are
incompatible with the Polish constitution, and that Polish courts need not
apply European law where the two collide.

**Zbigniew Ziobro**, who wanted the referral, calls it a reclamation of
sovereignty. The Commission calls it an attack on the foundation of the legal
order and starts preparing penalties. Nobody in the government has said the
word *Polexit* and the government has not proposed leaving anything, which is
exactly why the ruling is dangerous: it does not exit the Union, it simply
declares that the Union's law stops where a Polish court says it does.

A hundred thousand people are in the street within a week, mostly with European
flags and mostly organised by nobody in particular. It is the largest
spontaneous demonstration since the 2020 protests and it belongs to no party,
including ours.

[? if eu_veto_stance = "Backed conditionality": We spent last December
defending the rule-of-law mechanism against our own government, which makes
this month's position consistent and makes the sovereignty attack on us
older.?]
[? if eu_veto_stance = "Costed in delivery": Last December we refused the
sovereignty argument and priced the veto in hospitals and rail. The same
instrument is available now, and using it twice makes it our permanent method
rather than a tactic.?]
[? if eu_veto_stance = "Cross-camp guarantee": The channel we opened to Gowin's
wing last December is the only line into the governing camp that anybody in
this opposition possesses.?]
[? if nik_referral_channel = 1: Our audit-chamber referrals mean we can attach
a documented delivery number to the recovery money the ruling is about to
freeze.?]

- @oct21_common_front
- @oct21_material
- @oct21_dialogue
- @oct21_street

@oct21_common_front
title: Join one democratic defence of EU law
subtitle: Puts the Left inside a KO-led European front and lets the largest party define what the front is for.
on-arrival: ko_relation += 5; p2050_relation += 4; judicial_legitimacy += 5; constitutional_restraint += 3; rival_relation_ko_p2050 += 2; pis_relation -= 5; eu_relations += 5; news_headline = "The opposition answers the Tribunal with one European front"

= The constitutional fight gains a front, and an owner

Every democratic caucus signs one declaration and appears on one platform. The
Commission's officials, who have spent two years asking whether Polish
opposition parties can agree on anything, receive their answer.

The front is Tusk's. He called it, he speaks for it, and the flags in the
square are European rather than red. We have made the strongest available
defence of the legal order and simultaneously confirmed that the anti-PiS pole
has a single address, which is not ours.

