@turow_diplomacy
title: Send our own delegation to the Czech local authorities
subtitle: Treats a neighbour's water supply as a neighbour's problem; the government will call it working for a foreign state.
on-arrival: czech_relation += 14; eu_relations += 5; foreign_policy_capacity += 3; public_trust += 1; pis_relation -= 6; rural_support -= 2; news_headline = "Lewica deputies meet the Czech mayors the government refuses to see"

= Two towns discover they have the same problem

Our deputies go to Liberec and then to Bogatynia, in that order, and publish the
same set of questions in both places: whose measurements, whose wells, whose
compensation, whose deadline.

Government media runs the photographs for a week as evidence that the Left
represents Prague. What it actually produces is the first document in the
dispute that both sides' local officials agree is accurate, and a settlement
becomes possible several months earlier than it otherwise would.

- @october_2021_hub: Return to the October desk

@turow_sovereignty
title: Defend the mine and the jobs without conditions
subtitle: The position that holds the town; it puts us behind an unlawful licence and against a court we cite in every other fight.
on-arrival: workers_support += 4; rural_support += 5; social_patriot_support += 6; energy_security += 3; eu_relations -= 6; czech_relation -= 8; climate_state_capacity -= 4; judicial_legitimacy -= 4; institutional_trust -= 3; progressive_credibility -= 2; progressives_dissent += 6; razem_dissent += 4; news_headline = "The Left stands with Bogatynia and against the Court of Justice"

= The town keeps its answer and we lose our argument

In Bogatynia it lands. A party that has spent two years being told it despises
industrial workers turns up and says the pit stays open until there is
something to replace it, full stop.

In every other file we are handling — the Tribunal, the disciplinary chamber,
the recovery money — our case rests on Polish courts being bound by European
judgments. We have just told the country that this applies except when the
judgment reaches a town we like.

- @october_2021_hub: Return to the October desk

@turow_workers
title: Put the mine's own workforce between the two governments
subtitle: Refuses both nationalism and abstraction by making the union the negotiator; slower than either, and neither government wants it.
on-arrival: labor_credibility += 6; workers_support += 3; local_network += 3; movement_autonomy += 3; czech_relation += 4; eu_relations += 2; public_trust += 2; media_capacity += 1; news_headline = "The Turów workforce is given a seat in a dispute conducted over its head"

= The people in the pit acquire a delegation

We do not write the settlement. We fund the union's lawyers, get the workforce
formally admitted to the consultation, and insist that any agreement between
Warsaw and Prague carries the signature of somebody who works underground.

Neither government is pleased. The precedent survives them both: when the
licence question returns — and it returns — there is a workers' delegation with
standing, and it did not have to be invented in a crisis.

- @october_2021_hub: Return to the October desk

