The file we have been building since 2019 gets a second column: which councils
repealed, which kept funding the organisations that wrote the resolutions,
which still refuse a room to an equality group, and which have a named contact
for a harassment complaint.

Roughly a fifth changed something. The rest changed a vote. Publishing the
difference is the only thing that stops a repeal from being recorded as a
happy ending, and it is why the question is still live when the money
conditions expire.

