October closes with the congress settled and almost nothing else. A
Constitutional Tribunal has declared parts of the European treaties
inapplicable in Poland, half a million euro a day is running against Turów, and
the counties are rescinding their resolutions because Brussels reached them
before any Polish court did. The desk empties; the files do not.

